:: Castle Demon Book
<<effects>>

Looking around, you find an old book you don't think would be in a public library. It might make for an interesting read.
<br><br>

<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave the book alone|Castle]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Take the book|Demon Book Take]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Demon Book Take

You try to leave with the book in your hands. <span class="red">Something prevents you from leaving with the book.</span>
<br>
Instead, you decide to read it for clues as to what it is.
<br><br>

<<link [[Read the book|Demon Book Read]]>><</link>>

:: Demon Book Read

<<if $demonbookread is 1>>
    You decide to reread the demonic book. <span class="red">A voice in the back of your mind tells you this isn't a good idea, but you proceed anyways.</span>
    <br><br>
    You open the book. <span class="red"> A voice in the back of your mind tells you this isn't a good idea, but you proceed anyways.</span>
    <br><br>
    The book cautions of a dangerous ritual that only rewards the bravest of souls. To do this ritual, you must create a pentagram on the ground.
    <br>
    Next, you must say this chant: "Aithne, Aithne, Aithne, Sgeulachadh gu h-iubhair. Fionnlaigh, Fionnlaigh, Fionnlaigh, Sgeulachadh gu h-iubhair.."
    <br>
    The book does not say what will happen when you perform this ritual, or where this secret location is. Perhaps it's just fiction.
    <br><br>
<<else>>
    You open the book. <span class="red"> A voice in the back of your mind tells you this isn't a good idea, but you proceed anyways.</span>
    <br><br>
